---
description: Refresh the live design preview after every change
alwaysApply: true
---

Brandon reviews the site from the live preview, not from a description of the change.

The current URL is in `docs/live-previews.md`. After any visible change — type, layout, sections, flow, motion, navigation, or copy — run the applicable checks and commit. Then run `npm run preview:deliver -- /solutions/<affected-slug>/` (or the actual affected route). Pass every affected route when shared code changes. This command pushes the branch, waits for the public URL to serve the exact commit, and prints page links. Start the final response with those page links and the verified revision.

If the command exits nonzero, say the preview is stale and give the actual error. A local build or a successful push alone is not a live update. To check an already published commit without pushing, run `npm run preview:verify -- /solutions/<slug>/`.

Preview deployments of the working branch are authorized. Production release stays separate. If publication fails, report the preview as stale and name the blocker. Do not claim a deployed revision in `docs/live-previews.md` until it has been verified.
